Package: xfce4-caramos-plugin
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, caramos-ota, xfce4-panel
Description: CaramOS Control Center button and Show desktop strip for the Xfce panel
 The CaramOS Xfce taskbar shows the Control Center in its right island, as
 CaramOS Cinnamon does: the network, the volume and the battery, and a popup
 with sound, Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, VPN, power mode, dark mode, Night Light and the
 accent colour. The Control Center comes with caramos-ota; this plugin gives
 it its place in the panel.
 .
 Show desktop is a thin strip at the very end of the taskbar, after the right
 island: a click hides every window and shows the desktop, a second click
 brings them back, as on Windows and in Linux Mint.
